##### LED Effects — hardware/led_effects.cfg — ARCHIVED 2026-08-09 #####
#
# ARCHIVED: superseded by hardware/virtual_leds.cfg. Not included from printer.cfg anymore
# (see that file) — kept here for reference/rollback only. Switched to klipper-virtual_leds
# because its README documents this exact hardware pattern (Stealthburner-style status LED +
# separate nozzle LEDs on one chain) directly, its SET_LED semantics are a closer match to
# the original pre-led_effect NOZZLE_LIGHTS_ON/OFF design, and it writes straight into the
# shared chain state via Klipper's stock led.py helper rather than running its own
# independent render loop — no batching/ordering care needed the way led_effect required
# (see the [led_effect nozzle_lights] block below, and the printer.cfg comment on load
# order, both specific to led_effect's behavior, not virtual_leds'). klipper-led_effect
# itself is left installed/tracked (moonraker.conf's [update_manager led_effect]) in case
# it's wanted again for something animation-shaped later — this file just isn't loaded.
#
# klipper-led_effect (community addon — klippy/extras/led_effect.py, tracked via
# moonraker.conf's [update_manager led_effect]) split out of the single [neopixel _Toolhead]
# chain (thb:RGB, 3x GRBW: index 1 = status logo, index 2-3 = nozzle lights). Design notes
# from the research session that led here: ~/led_effects.md.
#
# Scope: nozzle lights (index 2-3) ONLY. Index 1 (status) stays exactly as it was, driven by
# macros/toolhead_leds.cfg's _SET_TH_LED/_STATUS_* — no [led_effect] object claims index 1,
# so there's no fight between led_effect's independent per-frame rendering and _SET_TH_LED's
# raw writes. Deliberate choice (the "Partial" migration option in led_effects.md) over
# wrapping status in led_effect too: status color is tied to live print-state logic
# (_STATUS_HOMING/_HEATING/_LEVELING/etc., changing constantly through PRINT_START), not
# something a Mainsail on/off toggle or a static effect layer fits well.
#
# Nozzle lights don't need RGB color — just brightness (INTENSITY) and a warm/cool tint
# (WARMTH), approximated on these GRBW LEDs by blending a little R (warm) or B (cool) on top
# of the W channel base, since there's no true CCT/dual-white hardware here.
#
# recalculate: true is required for SET_LED_EFFECT to accept INTENSITY/WARMTH params live —
# Mainsail's LED Effects panel (v2.17.0+) has no color/param picker, just on/off + a static
# swatch, so live tuning is via SET_LED_EFFECT from console/HA/Moonraker API, not the panel.
#
# Integration note (2026-08-09): _SET_TH_LED and _STATUS_OFF used to also write raw values
# to index 2-3 (re-asserting nozzle on/off state batched alongside index 1, to avoid flicker
# on the shared neopixel transmit) — exactly the kind of raw-SET_LED-vs-led_effect conflict
# this split has to avoid. Both were changed to leave index 2-3 alone entirely;
# NOZZLE_LIGHTS_ON/NOZZLE_LIGHTS_OFF and _STATUS_OFF now go through SET_LED_EFFECT
# exclusively for index 2-3. The old _NOZZLE_LIGHTS state-tracker macro is gone — this
# effect's own `enabled` status (printer["led_effect nozzle_lights"].enabled) is the single
# source of truth for nozzle-light state now, not a separately-tracked gcode variable.

[led_effect nozzle_lights]
autostart: false
recalculate: true
frame_rate: 24
leds:
    neopixel:_Toolhead (2-3)
layers:
    {% set intensity = params.INTENSITY|default(0.25)|float %}
    {% set warmth = params.WARMTH|default(0)|float %}
    {% set r = intensity * ([warmth, 0.0]|max) * 0.4 %}
    {% set b = intensity * ([-warmth, 0.0]|max) * 0.4 %}
    static 1 0 top ({r},0,{b},{intensity})
